{
  "summary": "Refactors block validation functions in `validation.cpp` to return `BlockValidationState` by value instead of returning `bool` with an out-parameter. Static factory methods `MakeInvalid` and `MakeError` are added to `BlockValidationState` for concise construction. Callers across `net_processing`, `bitcoinkernel`, RPC, storage, benchmarks, and tests are updated to inspect the returned state directly.",
  "problem": "Validation functions used a dual-reporting pattern returning a `bool` while populating a mutable `BlockValidationState&` reference. This allowed the boolean return and the state object to potentially diverge, created ambiguity about whether an incoming state was read or overwritten, and caused unintuitive behavior in chained calls where an already-invalid state suppresses recording subsequent error details.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: Follow-up to discussions in kernel PR #33856 regarding removing redundant return codes alongside validation states",
    "PR description: Eliminates the possibility that 'the bool return value and the returned state are inconsistent' and avoids 'unintuitive interaction between subsequent calls with the same state'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The 12 commits migrate individual functions bottom-to-top through the block validation call hierarchy (including `CheckBlock`, `AcceptBlock`, `AcceptBlockHeader`, and `FlushStateToDisk`).",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased with minor caller adjustments and an added test case for empty header processing in `test_empty_process_new_block_headers`.",
  "card": "This PR refactors core block validation functions—including CheckBlock, AcceptBlock, AcceptBlockHeader, and FlushStateToDisk—to return BlockValidationState by value rather than using a boolean return code and a mutable out-parameter. This eliminates the risk of divergent return statuses and prevents chained validation calls from silently dropping subsequent failure reasons into dirty state objects. Originating from libbitcoinkernel cleanups in PR 33856, the refactoring spans 12 commits ordered by call hierarchy and has no prerequisites.",
